<h2 id="descent-section-introduction" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="0239">35.1</span> Introduction</h2>

<p>
In the chapter on topologies on schemes (see Topologies, Section <a href="/tag/020L" data-tag="020L">34.1</a>) we introduced Zariski, étale, fppf, smooth, syntomic and fpqc coverings of schemes. In this chapter we discuss what kind of structures over schemes can be descended through such coverings. See for example <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-I">Gr-I</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-II">Gr-II</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-III">Gr-III</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-IV">Gr-IV</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-V">Gr-V</a>]</span>, and <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-VI">Gr-VI</a>]</span>. This is also meant to introduce the notions of descent, descent data, effective descent data, in the less formal setting of descent questions for quasi-coherent sheaves, schemes, etc. The formal notion, that of a stack over a site, is discussed in the chapter on stacks (see Stacks, Section <a href="/tag/0267" data-tag="0267">8.1</a>). 
</p>
